==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Power Cutter Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Neo Cutter Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Cutter Cat can be used as a second, stronger [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Express Cat]] against Red enemies, to quickly deal damage to long-ranged Red enemies when they're vulnerable for a few precious seconds or to quickly take out a Red frontliner. It strengthens its attack power when at 1% health (85,000 damage at level 30 with all [[Treasure]]s). At level 40, it can deal 110,000 damage and at level 50, deals 135,000 damage (to Red enemies). It has a 40-second recharge, so you'd better make it count.

Factoring in its Survive and Strengthen abilities, Cutter Cat will first deal 100% damage, then 500%, for a total of 6 times its base damage if it gets hit after every attack, so it is much more important to ensure that its second attack lands instead of the first.

Trying to intercept the attack of a [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance]] enemy is a viable strategy in some cases, so you can defend while letting it attack multiple times with the attack buff, rather than without.

==='''True Form'''===
Neo Cutter Cat increases its attack power, which is always welcome, and becomes [[Immune to Waves]], making sure the unit does not die on the way to [[Berserkory]] or [[Two Can]]. Overall, not a bad investment if you want a bit more mileage out of your Cutter Cat.

